; x86 stdcall build: the DLL exports the __stdcall-decorated wrappers
; (AdsXxx@N, from ace_stdcall_x86.c) instead of the plain AdsXxx names,
; because x86 MSVC cannot export both a plain name and the @N-decorated
; form of the same symbol (LNK4022 "cannot find unique match").
; Plain-name consumers link through the aliased import libraries.
LIBRARY
EXPORTS
; OpenADS ACE-compatible DLL exports.
; Reported by JONSSON RUSSI (RusSoft Ltda).
;
; All entry points use the Microsoft __cdecl convention (the SAP ACE
; default on Windows). Names are exported undecorated on x64 and x86;
; __cdecl on x86 prepends a leading underscore at link time, but the
; .def NAME form forces the public export to match the source name.
;
; NOTE: For x86 Harbour (rddads) compatibility, use openads_ace_x86.def
; which exports __stdcall-decorated (@N) names instead.
LIBRARY
EXPORTS
    oads_FOpen
    oads_FCreate
    oads_FClose
    oads_FRead
    oads_FWrite
    oads_FSeek
    oads_CheckExistence
    oads_DeleteFile
    oads_RenameFile
    oads_GetFileSize
    oads_GetFileTime
    oads_GetFileDate
    oads_DirMake
    oads_DirRemove
    oads_DirExist
    oads_Directory

    ; Legacy MSVC2013-era CRT shims (M8.2). Harbour's msvc64 prebuilt
    ; libs reference these symbols; modern UCRT no longer ships them.
    ; ace64.dll re-exports them under their legacy names so a Harbour
    ; app links cleanly without rebuilding Harbour.
    ;
    ; NOTE: _wfsopen is intentionally NOT exported here. Modern UCRT
    ; provides _wfsopen via api-ms-win-crt-stdio-l1-1-0.dll. Exporting
    ; it from the DLL caused STATUS_ENTRYPOINT_NOT_FOUND (0xC0000139)
    ; at load time: the PE loader resolved the DLL's own internal UCRT
    ; import of _wfsopen to its own export, creating a circular symbol
    ; that couldn't be located. See GitHub issue #N.
    _dclass   = openads_dclass
    _dsign    = openads_dsign
    _getch    = openads_getch
    _kbhit    = openads_kbhit
    _eof      = openads_eof

    ; M(rddads-compat) — extra Ads* entry points needed by Harbour
    ; contrib/rddads. Implemented as stubs in ace_exports.cpp;
    ; promoted here so the contrib links cleanly against ace64.lib.
    ; M12.22 — versioned ACE overloads bound by name from the X# RDD.
    ; Forwards to the base signatures (extra charset/collation/page-size
    ; params dropped); bookmark / property / find-by-name get a minimal
    ; implementation. See ace_exports.cpp.

    ; M12.23 — further entry points the X# Advantage RDD binds by name.

    ; RI property get/set.

    ; SAP ACE API name aliases — Add/Remove and permission variants used by SAP-built clients.

    ; Task 2: server-side filtered scan result-set API

    ; Tier-3: server-side aggregation result API

